---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { siteSettings } from '../lib/site';
const { contact, production, adsenseClient, amazonTag, tipUrl } = siteSettings();
const ads = production && Boolean(adsenseClient);
---
<Layout pageType="AboutPage" title="About — Who Goes First?" description="A small tool for the first decision of game night, with optional reveals and carefully reviewed starting-player rules."><div class="content-page prose"><h1>About</h1><p class="lede">Pick a starting player for your next game.</p><p>Use numbered seats when nobody wants to type. Add names if you like. Choose a method and pick a player. The selection works the same way in every presentation.</p><h2>Game rules</h2><p>A game’s starting instruction can differ by edition. Our directory publishes only records that have been checked against a publisher’s source and approved by a person. Missing rules stay missing until they’re reviewed.</p><p>Official instructions, our interpretation, and optional house rules are labeled separately. We’re an independent project, not affiliated with game publishers.</p><h2>No account needed</h2><p>No account, paid odds, or sign-up to see a result. Your group stays on your device. {ads ? <>Ads on rule and information pages keep the site free; the picker itself has no ads. See <a href="/privacy/">Privacy</a> for your choices.</> : <>The public site offers optional page visit analytics; see <a href="/privacy/">Privacy</a> for the choice.</>}</p>{(amazonTag || tipUrl) && <><h2>How the site is funded</h2><p>{amazonTag && <>Game pages may link to Amazon, and we earn a commission on qualifying purchases. </>}{tipUrl && <>You can also <a href={tipUrl} rel="noopener">support the site directly</a>. </>}Funding never decides which rules we publish or what they say.</p></>}<h2>Corrections & contact</h2><p>{contact ? <a href={`mailto:${contact}`}>{contact}</a> : 'This local build does not yet have an owner contact address. A maintained contact is required before public launch.'}</p><p>If a rule needs correcting, include the game, the edition, and a link to the publisher’s instruction. Don’t include your players’ names.</p><a class="inline-link" href="/">Back to the picker</a></div></Layout>

